46:    pixels are exactly coverable by four translated copies of one 2x2 sprite mask.
47:
48:    Rule
49:    Infer the unique 2x2 sprite mask whose four translated copies cover all
50:    foreground pixels without overlap, then stamp that mask into the upper-left,
51:    upper-right, lower-left, and lower-right 2x2 regions of a 5x5 output.
52:
53:    Key insight
54:    The tangled input arrangement is only a compact packing of four identical
55:    small sprites; the output regularizes the packing by inserting a blank middle
56:    row and column between the copies.
